1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,930
Arctis Obscura Forta Magnificat!

2
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:15,170
<i>I got 'im!</i>

3
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,210
Curious about what's going on down below?

4
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:25,060
A bit, yes.

5
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:29,310
Look, Guitane... 
enough's enough, how about we—

6
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:32,660
It seems my pawns have been depleted.

7
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,490
The Ten Commandments.

8
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:47,700
What the...?

9
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:52,190
The battle down there is not 
unlike the one up here.

10
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:56,840
Something fell from the sky.

11
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:00,830
Come on...

12
00:01:00,830 --> 00:01:02,290
You have to be kidding me.

13
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:05,460
I have sent...

14
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:08,430
Ten of my offspring to the surface.

15
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:15,800
All of them are chimeras with 
S-rankings in strength.

16
00:01:19,630 --> 00:01:25,620
I alone am more than sufficient 
to wipe this country out.

17
00:01:36,910 --> 00:01:41,830
I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince

18
00:01:36,910 --> 00:01:41,830
so I Can Take My Time
Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season

19
00:02:58,570 --> 00:03:03,540
Episode 23: The Battle Above the Clouds

20
00:02:59,230 --> 00:03:02,030
<i>I caught the mana of those eggs he launched.</i>

21
00:03:02,030 --> 00:03:04,020
<i>Now to intercept with Shadow Wolf.</i>

22
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:06,660
I'm afraid not.

23
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:12,160
It seems your method for using 
teleportation offensively...

24
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:16,000
requires a fair bit of focus.

25
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,500
And it's harder to hit moving targets, yes?

26
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,790
I won't allow you to meddle.

27
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:24,320
Galilea!

28
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:28,910
Until this nation is wiped off the map...

29
00:03:29,670 --> 00:03:32,430
My creations will not stop.

30
00:03:35,810 --> 00:03:37,900
What the hell is this thing?!

31
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:40,070
Run for it, Talia.

32
00:03:40,070 --> 00:03:42,000
This chimera...

33
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,940
It's not like the others!

34
00:03:47,190 --> 00:03:48,370
Open up!

35
00:03:48,370 --> 00:03:49,940
Let us out of here!

36
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:53,130
Hold on, everyone! You can't go outside! 
There are still a lot of chimeras—

37
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:55,820
How's it any safer in here, stupid?!

38
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:58,740
You want us to stand around 
while that thing eats us?!

39
00:04:01,830 --> 00:04:02,990
Guys!

40
00:04:02,990 --> 00:04:05,940
Miss Katarina! Get out of here, fast!

41
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:08,260
We'll hold this thing back!

42
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:10,880
But... you can't possibly...

43
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:14,250
What the hell is this?! I thought 
the church was supposed to be safe!

44
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:16,430
<i>We were already at our limit, and now...</i>

45
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:16,340
Why aren't the gods protecting us?!

46
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:18,270
Where's His Holiness?!

47
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:20,790
Where is God?!

48
00:04:21,670 --> 00:04:27,770
I can assure you, for the longest time, 
I believed they were out there.

49
00:04:30,730 --> 00:04:33,030
So, what do you say?

50
00:04:33,350 --> 00:04:37,630
Are you worthy of being called a god?

51
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:44,920
I keep telling you...!

52
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:48,920
The results make it obvious enough.

53
00:04:53,010 --> 00:04:54,310
Why...?

54
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:56,560
After everything we've been through...

55
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:58,850
Now we've gotta fight this thing?!

56
00:04:58,850 --> 00:05:01,810
You will be unable to 
protect a single thing...

57
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:07,160
Something's wrong! There's a huge 
swell of mana down on the surface!

58
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,070
What?!

59
00:05:10,470 --> 00:05:12,610
...as the country is destroyed.

60
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:20,890
Forgive me for being of no use.

61
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:27,710
For clarity's sake, I should point out that I 
have no intention of wiping out the people.

62
00:05:27,710 --> 00:05:30,720
It is the country that must be overthrown...

63
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:33,070
And its warped religion.

64
00:05:34,890 --> 00:05:39,850
For you see, the god at its 
foundation does not exist.

65
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:42,590
And I'm afraid that some casualties...

66
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:45,100
will be necessary...

67
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:49,100
for this revelation.

68
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,900
<i>Boundless Innocence.</i>

69
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:58,830
<i>The only Luxa that Escher can produce.</i>

70
00:06:59,450 --> 00:07:01,680
<i>Its offensive potential is virtually nil.</i>

71
00:07:02,270 --> 00:07:04,410
<i>Its effects... are amplification.</i>

72
00:07:05,310 --> 00:07:08,410
<i>Nothing more than a way of 
increasing the range of sound.</i>

73
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:12,460
<i>But with Escher's singing voice...</i>

74
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:15,600
<i>it can alleviate people's anxiety,</i>

75
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,390
<i>bolster their courage,</i>

76
00:07:19,290 --> 00:07:25,290
<i>and for a few moments, 
even take these mindless chimeras...</i>

77
00:07:31,350 --> 00:07:32,460
<i>and give them pause.</i>

78
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:35,900
<i>With one exception...</i>

79
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:39,020
<i>And that's me!</i>

80
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,560
Shadow Wolf

81
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:43,360
Shadow Wolf: Slash!

82
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:43,400
Slash

83
00:07:47,220 --> 00:07:50,930
Whatever made you start all this...

84
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:55,820
And whatever you've deluded 
yourself into believing I am...

85
00:07:56,510 --> 00:07:59,820
doesn't really matter at this 
point, and I can't say I care.

86
00:08:00,370 --> 00:08:03,250
My only interest is in your magic.

87
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:08,800
If I can take you in alive, you're welcome
to as much of my time as you want.

88
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,390
Don't worry.

89
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:18,540
Someone as myopic as you could never 
begin to grasp the depths of sorcery.

90
00:08:19,850 --> 00:08:20,970
Come on.

91
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,990
It's time for the final round.

92
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:31,040
I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince

93
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:31,040
so I Can Take My Time
Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season

94
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:33,910
What do you mean you're 
heading somewhere else?

95
00:08:33,910 --> 00:08:36,010
Situation's changed.

96
00:08:36,010 --> 00:08:37,920
This is just my gut talking, but...

97
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:39,700
This song is trouble.

98
00:08:40,680 --> 00:08:44,550
<i>The chimera's head exploded around 
the same time the song started.</i>

99
00:08:44,550 --> 00:08:46,750
<i>Was that divine intervention?</i>

100
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:49,790
<i>Whatever it was, 
there's no way he didn't notice.</i>

101
00:08:49,790 --> 00:08:52,020
I know the guy who made this mess.

102
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:55,490
So I won't be satisfied 
until all these chimera are dead.

103
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:58,300
<i>What a scary bishop...</i>

104
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,810
Dante, look out!

105
00:09:05,950 --> 00:09:08,690
Huh... Damn thing could still move.

106
00:09:08,690 --> 00:09:09,830
Sure could...

107
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:15,530
I'm headed towards the 
girl singing this song.

108
00:09:15,530 --> 00:09:17,540
You should stay here, miss.

109
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:20,070
No, I'll go too.

110
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:23,340
Escher's the one who's singing.

111
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:28,300
<i>Ever since learning the pope
was behind everything,</i>

112
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:31,150
<i>he suddenly started fighting ferociously.</i>

113
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:34,770
<i>I haven't been of any help ever since.</i>

114
00:09:34,770 --> 00:09:37,470
<i>Dante's done everything on his own.</i>

115
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:41,880
You've been looking out for the townspeople 
the whole time, haven't you?

116
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:46,260
You've been a lot more helpful 
than that clown on your back.

117
00:09:46,260 --> 00:09:48,790
You'd be right at home in the clergy, girl.

118
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:51,970
I could never...

119
00:09:51,970 --> 00:09:54,960
I like folks with a few 
skeletons in their closet.

120
00:09:58,910 --> 00:10:03,380
A touch of darkness is what 
makes us all human, y'know?

121
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:12,370
<i>That's right.</i>

122
00:10:13,330 --> 00:10:15,900
<i>I should've noticed way back when.</i>

123
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:21,170
<i>Boss Guitane... I'm gonna stop you.</i>

124
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:28,270
In those days, I was happy.

125
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:33,330
Papa, sing for me!

126
00:10:33,330 --> 00:10:35,530
Sure! But I'm tone deaf!

127
00:10:35,850 --> 00:10:39,870
It was a modest life, but I had a family.

128
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:44,360
They accepted me wholly, with no hesitation.

129
00:10:45,150 --> 00:10:47,330
I love your singing, Papa!

130
00:10:47,330 --> 00:10:50,040
His vocal sense is almost as 
bad as his sense of direction!

131
00:10:50,710 --> 00:10:54,040
They were what I cherished most.

132
00:10:54,330 --> 00:10:55,970
He's completely lost in his singing.

133
00:10:55,970 --> 00:10:57,600
But that's what it makes it so endearing.

134
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:00,100
And as if in response to that happiness,

135
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:05,970
countless faithful would show up at the 
church for me to cast divine sorcery on.

136
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:10,850
You there. I believe your name is Guitane?

137
00:11:10,850 --> 00:11:13,490
That voice... is that you, Angel Jihriel?!

138
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:17,920
Even an angel came to encourage me.

139
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:21,520
I hear your singing every day 
up here, and it's obnoxious.

140
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:23,110
You really can't carry a note.

141
00:11:23,110 --> 00:11:25,640
I-I'm sorry. But...

142
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:29,540
I know. There are many 
humans who rely on you.

143
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:32,140
But, you needn't sing any longer.

144
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:36,370
You'll be able to use divine 
sorcery freely from now on.

145
00:11:37,890 --> 00:11:42,160
I'm giving you a personal pass. 
You should consider it an honor.

146
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:44,130
Thank you so much!

147
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:49,260
After becoming a bishop, 
I was tested time and again...

148
00:11:49,260 --> 00:11:52,160
Go ahead and try and purify me, pal.

149
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:54,790
You're not gonna see any change.

150
00:11:54,790 --> 00:11:57,520
<i>These kinds of confrontations 
got on my nerves...</i>

151
00:12:00,580 --> 00:12:03,190
So I would use Luxa to clobber 
the ones who started them.

152
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:05,340
What about the purification...?

153
00:12:05,340 --> 00:12:09,380
Because it looked like you were hoping 
to use purification as a shortcut

154
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:11,410
to escape the darkness inside you.

155
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:13,330
You needn't rely on purification.

156
00:12:14,170 --> 00:12:19,240
I'm sure you can overcome 
those dark impulses.

157
00:12:21,340 --> 00:12:24,720
Boss Guitane! I decided to 
go for a look like yours!

158
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:28,180
Could you please not refer 
to me like that, Dante?

159
00:12:28,930 --> 00:12:34,190
He was my best friend, 
and surrogate brother.

160
00:12:34,190 --> 00:12:36,540
I'm trying to tell you!

161
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:41,380
Once I become king, I can actually 
do something about poverty!

162
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:43,730
Then could you please do it already?!

163
00:12:43,730 --> 00:12:48,450
There are still people on the outskirts 
of Saloum who are suffering!

164
00:12:48,450 --> 00:12:52,460
There were times I even 
clashed with royalty...

165
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:56,220
Then you need to become pope! 
It's only fair!

166
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:59,560
Yet I had nothing to fear, in spite of that.

167
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:03,460
Let us both aim for greater heights, 
to make the country a better place!

168
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:07,730
Because I had a foundation 
of faith in my soul.

169
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:10,750
Until it happened...

170
00:13:11,470 --> 00:13:16,810
There was malnourished little girl 
sitting in front of my house.

171
00:13:16,810 --> 00:13:21,470
It was obvious at a glance that she had 
came from the poverty-stricken slums.

172
00:13:21,470 --> 00:13:27,900
I invited her inside at once. I had intended 
to feed her some of my wife's cooking.

173
00:13:27,900 --> 00:13:31,020
I thought she might make 
a good friend for my son.

174
00:13:32,490 --> 00:13:37,560
This girl, named Anastasia, 
muttered the oddest thing...

175
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:40,890
Daddy said to keep watch outside.

176
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:48,760
It was obvious in an instant what she meant.

177
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:53,540
My family lied in pools of their own blood.

178
00:13:57,090 --> 00:14:01,220
And right across from the bodies 
of my wife and child was a man,

179
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:04,290
gorging himself on any food he could find.

180
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:10,570
"Who is this filth? 
Why didn't God protect my family?"

181
00:14:10,570 --> 00:14:13,900
"Why am I even serving Him?"

182
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:17,920
By the time the coiling chain 
of hatred led me to an answer,

183
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:20,310
I found myself in even deeper despair.

184
00:14:20,790 --> 00:14:26,040
Had I been serving God... 
while hoping to be rewarded?

185
00:14:33,350 --> 00:14:38,050
I finally found the resolve to purify him.

186
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:42,450
What kind of penitence would he offer?

187
00:14:42,450 --> 00:14:45,940
And would it be enough to forgive him?

188
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:51,440
But in the next moment, my anxiety 
over these answers was wiped away.

189
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:58,460
He did not repent. He did not do anything, 
except continue to stuff his mouth.

190
00:14:58,850 --> 00:15:03,130
In confusion, I continued to shine 
the light of purification on him.

191
00:15:03,130 --> 00:15:08,350
My anger had given way 
to fear, at that point.

192
00:15:10,010 --> 00:15:14,330
In the end... he simply died.

193
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:16,980
He had starved to death.

194
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:25,720
The purity of this act. 
It was nothing more than hunger.

195
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:27,460
And so, he ate.

196
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:30,270
Killing my family to do it.

197
00:15:30,870 --> 00:15:32,420
"Is this a joke?"

198
00:15:32,420 --> 00:15:35,860
Is purity of intent enough 
to excuse anything?

199
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:40,370
I'm sorry... I'm so sorry...

200
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:38,990
Is that how the gods define evil?

201
00:15:38,990 --> 00:15:42,940
Then wouldn't the purest of heart...

202
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:46,410
those who are closest 
to being true saints...

203
00:15:46,410 --> 00:15:48,750
be monsters?

204
00:15:48,750 --> 00:15:50,500
Bishop Guitane.

205
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:52,750
Boss Guitane.

206
00:15:53,130 --> 00:15:57,370
I'm so sorry... I'm so sorry!

207
00:15:56,390 --> 00:15:57,760
Guitane.

208
00:15:57,760 --> 00:16:02,470
I vaguely remember being talked 
at by many people, afterwards.

209
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:08,650
To tell the truth, the responses I gave 
at the time made me want to vomit.

210
00:16:09,150 --> 00:16:14,540
I am a pastor. This is the symbol 
of that faith. Trust in God.

211
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:20,540
I am a pastor. This is the symbol 
of that faith. Trust in God...

212
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:22,760
But even that sense of revulsion, in time, 
sunk into the darkness before dissolving.

213
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:27,290
I am a pastor. This is the symbol 
of that faith. Trust in God...

214
00:16:23,110 --> 00:16:27,290
People called me a saint for how I behaved.

215
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:32,050
The light was unable to purge my darkness.

216
00:16:32,470 --> 00:16:38,440
I was certain of it then: that this 
swirling vortex within me was not evil.

217
00:16:39,110 --> 00:16:42,430
O God... I take it you have no objections?

218
00:16:42,430 --> 00:16:45,310
Because if it is righteous...

219
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:49,980
then I will unleash this impulse 
I feel, with no restraint.

220
00:16:51,070 --> 00:16:54,900
This pristine darkness.

221
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:07,520
After that, I sought out monsters to—

222
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:08,470
Enough already.

223
00:17:08,470 --> 00:17:10,770
What's with the whole life story?

224
00:17:10,770 --> 00:17:12,520
Can you not see the face 
I'm making over here?

225
00:17:13,020 --> 00:17:14,950
Your story is depressing. And long.

226
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:16,880
And it's turned things 
monochrome for some reason.

227
00:17:18,130 --> 00:17:21,590
I dunno what you expect a 7th 
Prince to do with all that!

228
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,350
Yes. I know.

229
00:17:24,350 --> 00:17:27,360
I can only imagine that a story like this...

230
00:17:27,690 --> 00:17:30,100
must make the ears of a god, 
such as yourself, burn.

231
00:17:32,130 --> 00:17:36,460
Which is precisely why you must hear it.

232
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:40,390
The story of everything
that's led to this point!

233
00:17:40,390 --> 00:17:43,120
And you are obligated 
to answer my questions!

234
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:44,240
Yeah, whatever.

235
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:46,610
I hear you, so let's get on with it.

236
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:50,200
Are gods so truly...

237
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:53,140
reluctant to listen to reason?!

238
00:17:53,130 --> 00:17:56,140
WHACK

239
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:56,130
I don't wanna hear that from you, man!

240
00:17:57,630 --> 00:17:59,860
What an incredible singing voice.

241
00:17:59,860 --> 00:18:03,610
The singing saint, Escher, 
has blessed us with a miracle!

242
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:06,130
Let's hang in there, people!

243
00:18:06,130 --> 00:18:08,190
Sister Escher's singing for us!

244
00:18:08,940 --> 00:18:12,160
Hey! Babylon! Where are you headed?!

245
00:18:12,410 --> 00:18:16,010
And what is this song?! 
It's getting way more attention than me!

246
00:18:16,010 --> 00:18:19,300
You're right! The people stopped 
panicking the second they heard it!

247
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:22,360
It even made the heads of those chimeras 
who fell from the sky explode!

248
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:25,740
God has answered our prayers with this song!

249
00:18:26,190 --> 00:18:29,420
<i>No. I'm pretty sure our boss 
took out the chimeras.</i>

250
00:18:29,890 --> 00:18:33,690
<i>And this static I can hear...</i>

251
00:18:34,130 --> 00:18:36,260
<i>Don't push yourself too hard, Escher.</i>

252
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:40,640
<i>This song is the thing that's 
keeping people's spirits intact.</i>

253
00:18:43,190 --> 00:18:45,410
<i>If the singing stops...</i>

254
00:18:45,410 --> 00:18:47,620
<i>There'd be no way to stop the chaos.</i>

255
00:18:50,710 --> 00:18:51,760
<i>Which is why...</i>

256
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:58,410
<i>we won't stop.</i>

257
00:18:59,290 --> 00:19:01,100
<i>When this song is over...</i>

258
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:05,080
<i>When this battle is over...</i>

259
00:19:05,830 --> 00:19:08,300
<i>When the seemingly endless 
rain finally dries up,</i>

260
00:19:09,610 --> 00:19:11,160
<i>a rainbow will shine.</i>

261
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:14,470
<i>We have faith!</i>

262
00:19:15,340 --> 00:19:18,690
Uwaaaah

263
00:19:23,650 --> 00:19:26,830
Doesn't Escher have the best singing voice?

264
00:19:27,430 --> 00:19:29,190
My sister's doing great, too!

265
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:32,240
They sound a lot sharper than 
they did during rehearsal.

266
00:19:33,390 --> 00:19:37,810
Y'know... there's one thing I wanted 
to show you, more than anything else.

267
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:39,570
What are you—

268
00:19:40,830 --> 00:19:42,500
<i>What is this?!</i>

269
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:45,030
I'm going to launch this 
in time with the song.

270
00:19:45,030 --> 00:19:46,610
Listen closely, okay?

271
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:58,590
<i>What just happened?! 
Some application of his teleportation?!</i>

272
00:19:58,590 --> 00:20:00,840
<i>No, there was always lag when he used that!</i>

273
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:05,590
Concealment and sorcery. 
Full Sprint and sorcery.

274
00:20:05,590 --> 00:20:10,230
Magic that can't physically be seen, 
and magic that's too fast to be seen.

275
00:20:10,230 --> 00:20:12,360
Basic but nasty, isn't it?

276
00:20:12,830 --> 00:20:14,620
Celero Cascadia.

277
00:20:15,110 --> 00:20:16,610
Kryptis Incinis.

278
00:20:17,230 --> 00:20:18,240
ZWOM

279
00:20:17,620 --> 00:20:18,240
ZWOM

280
00:20:22,030 --> 00:20:25,920
The water blast was moving so fast, 
it froze! That's hilarious.

281
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:30,050
<i>Stealth magic where the first reaction 
is the impact of it landing?!</i>

282
00:20:30,050 --> 00:20:30,990
<i>But...</i>

283
00:20:31,470 --> 00:20:32,750
<i>It's pointless!</i>

284
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:36,350
<i>I'm going to utilize your power, Civil War!</i>

285
00:20:37,130 --> 00:20:39,090
<i>Spinal Shield!</i>

286
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:45,000
<i>Good! I'm able to react to it...</i>

287
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:48,490
Krypta Celero Lithis!

288
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:48,390
WHA-BAM

289
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:52,370
Wow, you can use the spinal threads too?!

290
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:54,820
Now I really wanna take you alive!

291
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:59,540
<i>I was barely able to react in time, but he's 
able to launch too many attacks at once!</i>

292
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:01,770
<i>I need to focus more!</i>

293
00:21:01,770 --> 00:21:04,610
<i>Focus!</i>

294
00:21:07,610 --> 00:21:09,290
<i>Shut up!</i>

295
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:14,050
Mana Focus:
Seven Goddesses

296
00:21:10,710 --> 00:21:13,700
Mana Focus: Seven Goddesses.

297
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:16,780
<i>What is this?!</i>

298
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:20,630
<i>The spinal threads were severed 
before I could even react!</i>

299
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:24,840
<i>A density of mana so great 
that Luxa loses its luster?!</i>

300
00:21:25,370 --> 00:21:29,900
Someone as myopic as you could never 
begin to grasp the depths of sorcery.

301
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:31,690
<i>This is...</i>

302
00:21:32,730 --> 00:21:38,690
<i>Are my decades of life really going to 
be denied by this inexplicable... thing?!</i>

303
00:21:39,130 --> 00:21:44,440
<i>By this... demonic, maniacal... absurdity?!</i>

304
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:47,370
Come to think of it, 
you said something before...

305
00:21:48,260 --> 00:21:51,200
About how there's nothing to be 
gained by targeting your heart.

306
00:21:51,610 --> 00:21:54,390
Let's test that theory.

307
00:21:58,190 --> 00:21:59,460
God?!

308
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:00,960
Glow.

309
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:41,060
<i>The 7th Prince. Is he a god?
Or an innocent devil?</i>

310
00:23:41,490 --> 00:23:43,860
<i>Next time, on Episode 24:</i>

311
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:45,570
<i>"In the Light."</i>

312
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:49,160
Episode 24

313
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:49,160
In the Light

314
00:23:45,570 --> 00:23:50,000
<i>You will witness the depths of sorcery.</i>

